      "[Expert R1] (Detect atomicity violations in the code.)\n```json\n{\n    \"violations\": [\n        {\n            \"sharedVariable\": \"data2\",\n            \"accessPattern\": [\"Read\", \"Write\", \"Write\"],\n            \"lines\": [10, 20, 11]\n        },\n        {\n            \"sharedVariable\": \"data1\",\n            \"accessPattern\": [\"Read\", \"Write\", \"Write\"],\n            \"lines\": [8, 18, 9]\n        }\n    ]\n}\n```\n\n[System] Expert first round completed in 4.64 seconds\n\n[Judge R1] (Validate the expert's defect report and check control/interrupt conditions.)\nLet me analyze each read/write operation for the global variables `data1` and `data2`.\n\n## Step 1: Check Control Conditions\n\n### Operations in `svp_simple_324_001_isr_1`:\n- Line 8: `int tmp = data1 + 1;` (Read of data1)\n- Line 9: `data1 = tmp;` (Write to data1)\n- Line 10: `int tmp1 = data2 + 1;` (Read of data2)\n- Line 11: `data2 = tmp1;` (Write to data2)\n\nThese operations are not guarded by any control conditions - they will execute whenever `svp_simple_324_001_isr_1` is triggered.\n\n### Operations in `svp_simple_324_001_isr_2`:\n- Line 17: `int tmp = data1 + 5;` (Read of data1)\n- Line 18: `data1 = tmp;` (Write to data1)\n- Line 19: `int tmp1 = data2 + 5;` (Read of data2)\n- Line 20: `data2 = tmp1;` (Write to data2)\n\nThese operations are not guarded by any control conditions - they will execute whenever `svp_simple_324_001_isr_2` is triggered.\n\n### Operations in `svp_simple_324_001_main`:\n- Line 27: `data1 = 10;` (Write to data1)\n- Line 28: `data2 = 10;` (Write to data2)\n- Line 30: `if (data1==16 && data2==5)` (Read of data1 and data2)\n\nThe reads at line 30 are part of a control condition. Let me analyze if this condition can be satisfied:\n- `data1` is initialized to 10 at line 27\n- `data2` is initialized to 10 at line 28\n- There are no interrupt handlers enabled or disabled in the main function\n- Without any ISRs being triggered, `data1` and `data2` will remain 10\n- Therefore, the condition `data1==16 && data2==5` will always be false\n- The ERROR block at lines 31-33 will never be executed\n\n## Step 2: Pay Attention to Control Condition Changes\n\nThere are no operations in the code that change control conditions. The ISRs don't modify any variables that would affect the control flow of other functions.\n\n## Step 3: Check Interrupt Status\n\nThe code does not contain any `disable_isr()` or `enable_isr()` calls. This means:\n- All interrupts are enabled by default\n- Both `svp_simple_324_001_isr_1` and `svp_simple_324_001_isr_2` can preempt the main function\n- The ISRs can also preempt each other based on their priorities (ISR1 has priority 1, ISR2 has priority 2)\n\n## Step 4: Generate Final Report\n\n### Summary of Analysis:\n1. **data1 operations**:\n   - Read at line 8 (ISR1) - can execute when ISR1 preempts\n   - Write at line 9 (ISR1) - can execute when ISR1 preempts\n   - Read at line 17 (ISR2) - can execute when ISR2 preempts\n   - Write at line 18 (ISR2) - can execute when ISR2 preempts\n   - Write at line 27 (main) - can execute in main\n\n2. **data2 operations**:\n   - Read at line 10 (ISR1) - can execute when ISR1 preempts\n   - Write at line 11 (ISR1) - can execute when ISR1 preempts\n   - Read at line 19 (ISR2) - can execute when ISR2 preempts\n   - Write at line 20 (ISR2) - can execute when ISR2 preempts\n   - Write at line 28 (main) - can execute in main\n\nAll read/write operations can potentially execute, so the atomicity violations reported are valid.\n\n```json\n{\n    \"violations\": [\n        {\n            \"sharedVariable\": \"data2\",\n            \"accessPattern\": [\"Read\", \"Write\", \"Write\"],\n            \"lines\": [10, 20, 11]\n        },\n        {\n            \"sharedVariable\": \"data1\",\n            \"accessPattern\": [\"Read\", \"Write\", \"Write\"],\n            \"lines\": [8, 18, 9]\n        }\n    ]\n}\n```\n\n[Expert R2] (Refine the report based on judge feedback, 